  ch1p1: 'A sundial reads the sun’s position, and the sun does not keep a steady pace. In January the Earth is nearest the sun and hurries along its path; in July it lingers. The lean of the axis stretches and squeezes the sun’s daily progress a second time. Add the two and you get the equation of time: the sun is up to sixteen minutes early in early November and fourteen minutes late in mid-February. Only four days a year does it agree with the clock.',
